msgid ""
"The KDE Wallet system stores your data in a <i>wallet</i>"
" file on your local hard disk.  The data is only written in encrypted form, "
"presently using the blowfish algorithm with your password as the key.  When "
"a wallet is opened, the wallet manager application will launch and display "
"an icon in the system tray.  You can use this application to manage your "
"wallets.  It even permits you to drag wallets and wallet contents, allowing "
"you to easily copy a wallet to a remote system."
